  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rockwell Collins has $341M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 556 awards, with an average award size of $613K. Obligations fell 63.2% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $340M of the current-year total, making the DoD Rockwell Collins's dominant buyer so far this fiscal year. Top markets by obligation are Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $98.5M, Engineering Services at $88.1M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $62.2M. Other notable markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $41.2M, Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $33.3M, and Explosives Manufacturing at $11.5M. Historical obligations show a peak of $1B in FY24 and a decline to $341M in FY26. These figures are fiscal-year-to-date totals and represent contract obligations unless otherwise noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Rockwell Collins's FY2026 obligations by buyer?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $340M, so the DoD accounts for nearly all FY2026 obligations. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $852K, with all other agencies accounting for the remainder. That makes FY2026 obligations highly concentrated with a single agency."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets dominate Rockwell Collins's federal sales?",
        "body": "Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing leads with $98.5M in obligations. Engineering Services follows with $88.1M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing with $62.2M. Other significant markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $41.2M and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $33.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
